( Stateless coordinate hash for procedural grids, with no dependencies. )
( All inputs are unsigned bytes. X and Y each wrap modulo 256. )
( The seed selects a deterministic permutation of the 16-bit input. )
( Keeping the full word preserves the permutation; use the high byte )
( when only one byte is needed. No mutable memory or devices. )

@hash2d/word ( x y seed -- hash** )
    #9d MUL DUP #a7 EOR EOR2
    DUP2 #07 SFT2 EOR2 #2c1b MUL2
    DUP2 #05 SFT2 EOR2 #297b MUL2
    DUP2 #09 SFT2 EOR2 JMP2r
